## Data Files

### `data/heightmap-templates.js`

Contains heightmap template definitions. Each template is a string of newline-separated steps:

```javascript
const heightmapTemplates = {
  continents: {
    name: "Continents",
    template: `Hill 3 20-40 10-90 10-90
Range 2 30-60 20-80 20-80
Pit 1 10-20 30-70 30-70`
  },
  // ... more templates
};
```

**Step Format:** `Tool count height-range x-range y-range`

**Tools:**
- `Hill` - Add hills
- `Pit` - Add depressions
- `Range` - Add mountain ranges
- `Trough` - Add valleys
- `Strait` - Carve straits
- `Mask` - Apply edge mask
- `Invert` - Invert heightmap
- `Add` - Add to heights
- `Multiply` - Multiply heights
- `Smooth` - Smooth heights

---

## Rendering

The included `index.html` renders the generated map to a canvas:

```javascript
function drawMap(map, ctx) {
  const { pack } = map;
  const biomes = pack.biomes;
  const cells = pack.cells;
  const scale = Math.min(MAX_W / graphWidth, MAX_H / graphHeight);

  ctx.clearRect(0, 0, MAX_W, MAX_H);
  ctx.fillStyle = biomes[0].color;  // Ocean color
  ctx.fillRect(0, 0, MAX_W, MAX_H);

  for (let i = 0; i < cells.i.length; i++) {
    const biomeId = cells.biome[i];
    const color = biomes[biomeId].color;
    const poly = getPackPolygon(i);
    
    ctx.beginPath();
    for (let j = 0; j < poly.length; j++) {
      const [x, y] = poly[j];
      const sx = x * scale;
      const sy = y * scale;
      if (j === 0) ctx.moveTo(sx, sy);
      else ctx.lineTo(sx, sy);
    }
    ctx.closePath();
    ctx.fillStyle = color;
    ctx.fill();
  }
}
```

